The audience is first-time, never-licensed Vermont applicants, typically teenagers on the learner's permit and junior license path and adults applying for a first driver's license, reading at a plain-English level with no assumed driving vocabulary. This section teaches that impairment includes drugs and drowsiness as well as alcohol, the adult and under twenty-one blood alcohol thresholds, the six ways alcohol degrades driving, that only time sobers, the implied consent law and its refusal penalty, how to plan before drinking, and how to recognize and respond to drowsiness. The content assumes no prior rule knowledge and no prerequisites beyond literacy; every term the section introduces is defined in the glossary lines of part C.
